From: Sirius port
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] clk: qcom: krait-cc: fix the aux parent name on v2

krait_cc_probe() registers the shared aux clock as "acpu_aux":

	clk = clk_register_fixed_factor(dev, "acpu_aux", "gpll0_vote", 0, 1, 2);

but krait_add_sec_mux() asks for it as "apu_aux" on the same path:

	} else {
		sec_mux_list[1].name = "apu_aux";
	}

The unique_aux branch above it (krait-cc-v1, which takes per-CPU aux clocks
from the device tree) spells the name correctly, so only v2 is affected.
With the name as it stands the secondary mux cannot resolve its second
parent, which is the path the driver switches to while reprogramming an
HFPLL.

No in-tree device tree uses qcom,krait-cc-v1 or -v2 -- none defines the
clock controller at all -- so this has not been reachable until now.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/krait-cc.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/krait-cc.c
@@ -191,7 +191,7 @@ krait_add_sec_mux(struct device *dev, int id, const char *s,
 		sec_mux_list[1].fw_name = parent_name;
 		sec_mux_list[1].name = parent_name;
 	} else {
-		sec_mux_list[1].name = "apu_aux";
+		sec_mux_list[1].name = "acpu_aux";
 	}
 
 	ret = devm_clk_hw_register(dev, &mux->hw);
